  "_source_stem": "Merrimac2024",
  "_notes": "Precinct-level (P1 306 / P2 253). Labelled PRELIMINARY by the clerk. SELECTMAN IS ONE VOTE-FOR-THREE RACE, not three races: the ballot prints term lengths beside the names (Bruno 3 Years, Adams 2 Years, Gustison 1 Year) and the column totals 1,677 = 559 x 3, so the term follows the vote rank and Hatch is the loser. The two ASSESSOR blocks are distinct seats -- each closes on 559 alone. The scanned PDF at the citation has no text layer; rendered and OCR'd at 250 dpi its header reads 'Preliminary Results Local Election 5.6.2024' and its figures match the clerk's .xlsx workbook exactly, so the two are one source in two formats and not independent corroboration. All eleven races close on 559. NAME GROUNDING: 15 of 17 surnames appear in the 250-dpi OCR of the hosted scan. The two that do not are OCR corruption, not parse error -- the scan renders Ashlyn Calgani as \"Ashlyn Ca'gani\" and Susan Coburn as \"Susan Courn\". Both are spelled correctly in the clerk's own .xlsx workbook, which is the parse source and carries the identical figures.",
